<h2><strong>Annex III – Specific Conditions of Level 3: Validator </strong></h2>
<details>
<summary>See Annex III </summary>
<ol>
<li>
<h3><strong>Applicability: </strong></h3>
<p>This Annex III will govern in the event that the Participant is
                selected and authorized as Validator of the ISBE network. The subscription
                of this annex accredits the Participant to operate a Consensus Node
                in the ISBE infrastructure, with the rights and responsibilities that
                it implies. </p>
</li>
<li>
<h3><strong>Purpose of the Annex: </strong></h3>
<p>Establish the particular conditions under which the
                Participant will perform the Validator Participation Level,
                considered critical for the security and operation of the ISBE network,
                participate in the consensus and validation mechanism
                transactions. </p>
<p>This annex complements the Framework Contract by specifying commitments
                technical, service levels and economic compensations associated with the
                operation of a Consensus Node. </p>
</li>
<li>
<h3><strong>Qualification as Validator: </strong></h3>
<p>To qualify for the Validator Participation Level, the Participant
                you must: <em><strong>(Yo) </strong></em>be an active Core Participant
                and fulfill its obligations to the satisfaction of the Managing Entity; <em><strong>(ii) </strong></em>demonstrate technical capacity and resources
                sufficient to operate a validator node in accordance with the
                specifications of Policy INF1040 (hardware requirements,
                connectivity, security); <em><strong>(iii) </strong></em>overcome the
                technical tests that the Managing Entity deems necessary ( <em>e.g. </em>connectivity testing in a <em>testnet </em>); and <em><strong>(iv) </strong></em>sign this annex, formalizing
                their commitment to act diligently in the validation tasks and
                comply with the operational guidelines given. </p>
<p>The Managing Entity, after evaluating compliance with the
                requirements described above and depending on the needs of the
                ISBE network, will approve the incorporation of the Participant to the set of
                authorized validators. </p>
<p>You will be provided with keys, certificates or <em>whitelist </em>necessary for your Consensus Node to be recognized by the ISBE network
                (process of <em>permitted </em>of its node), as well as the information
                configuration (addresses) <em>bootnodes </em>, QBFT parameters,
                etc.). </p>
<p>The Participant will join either as an active validator or in status
                waiting ( <em>standby </em>), according to the rotation scheme in force in
                every moment. </p>
</li>
<li>
<h3><strong>Obligations of the Validator: </strong></h3>
<ol type="a">
<li>
<p><em><u>Consensus Node Operation </u></em>: The Participant
                        undertakes to operate a Consensus Node of the ISBE network in a manner
                        continuous and in accordance with the established technical specifications. This
                        involves enabling a dedicated execution environment, with <em>hardware </em>and <em>software </em>approved ( <em>e.g. </em>run a client <em>Hyperledger Besu </em>in approved version), and
                        keep it running 24/7 to participate in the validation of
                        blocks. </p>
<p>You must implement all bastion and cybersecurity measures
                        indicated in policy INF1040, such as: <em><strong>(Yo) </strong></em>isolation of the machine (not running
                        unnecessary services); <em><strong>(ii) </strong></em>configuration in
                        secure network ( <em>firewalls </em>, opening only required ports); <em><strong>(iii) </strong></em>validation key protection
                        (secure storage, possibly with HSM); and <em><strong>(iv) </strong></em>timely update of <em>software </em>when security patches are released. </p>
<p>You must also follow the instructions on rotation between states
                        active and passive of its Consensus Node if the governance so determines
                        to balance participation. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><em><u>Availability and performance </u></em>: The Participant
                        You must maintain a high level of availability of your Consensus Node,
                        looking for a <em>uptime </em>close to 100% and minimizing latency
                        in the signing and transmission of blocks. </p>
<p>Policy INF1040 defines Service Level Agreements
                        (“ <strong>SLAs </strong>") specific ( <em>e.g. </em>a percentage
                        minimum number of signed blocks and a maximum tolerated latency) that the
                        Participant agrees to comply. </p>
<p>Currently, reference metrics are established such as: <em><strong>(Yo) </strong></em>monthly availability &gt; 99%; <em><strong>(ii) </strong></em>absence of long disconnections; <em><strong>(iii) </strong></em>signing of at least [●]% of shifts
                        assigned validation, etc. These metrics are monitored
                        constantly through the system <em>health-check </em>from ISBE. The
                        Participant accepts that said metrics are recorded and used
                        to evaluate its performance, agreeing that the Managing Entity
                        access the data of your Consensus Node necessary for said
                        monitoring. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><em><u>Active participation in the consensus </u></em>:The
                        Participant will act diligently in the proposal and signing of blocks
                        under the QBFT algorithm (Istanbul BFT using ISBE). </p>
<p>You must not unjustifiably refuse to validate transactions or
                        introduce deliberate delays. </p>
<p>If for any technical reason you need to pause your participation (for
                        maintenance, for example), will coordinate it with the Managing Entity to
                        be temporarily replaced or put on standby status <em>standby </em>without
                        affect the <em>quorum </em>validation. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><em><u>Limitations and proper use </u></em>: The Participant does not
                        will use your Consensus Node for purposes other than validation. In
                        Specifically, you are prohibited from using it to deploy contracts
                        intelligent, to serve general network read traffic or to
                        connect it to corporate systems of the Participant other than the
                        monitoring it. </p>
<p>The Consensus Node must remain in the location and conditions
                        declared; any material change ( <em>e.g. </em>move it from center
                        change significant settings) must be notified and
                        may require a new inspection or approval. </p>
<p>If the Participant wishes to temporarily or permanently cease the
                        operation of its Consensus Node, it will communicate it in advance
                        sufficient (except force majeure) for the Managing Entity to take measures
                        (e.g. appoint a new Validator in its place). </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><em><u>INF1040 Compliance </u></em>: In general, the
                        Participant will comply with all applicable sections of the Policy
                        INF1040, which are considered reproduced here. In summary: <em><strong>(Yo) </strong></em>keep updated <em>software </em>to the required version; <em><strong>(ii) </strong></em>apply
                        recommended security settings; <em><strong>(iii) </strong></em>attend to monitoring alerts
                        ( <em>e.g. </em>If your Consensus Node falls behind in height
                        block or presents synchronization errors, you must intervene
                        immediate); and <em><strong>(iv) </strong></em>respect the procedures
                        of depermission in case of cessation (the Consensus Node will be eliminated
                        from the list of validators in an ordered manner). </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><em><u>Collaboration with technical governance </u></em>:The
                        Participant will participate, to the extent possible, in meetings or
                        validator technical forums that the Managing Entity convenes to
                        coordinate improvements, discuss performance parameters or other aspects
                        of the network's operation. In addition, the Participant will contribute
                        truthful information about your Consensus Node when required to
                        diagnoses ( <em>e.g. </em> <em>logs </em>relevant to a
                        incident). </p>
<p>If you are prompted to implement any configuration changes or patches
                        urgent for security reasons, the Participant will do so without delay
                        following the instructions provided. </p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>
<h3><strong>Remuneration and costs: </strong></h3>
<p>In order to encourage the contribution of Validators and compensate
                the dedicated resources, ISBE provides for periodic financial compensation
                to the Participant for the operation of its Consensus Node, conditioned on the
                Satisfactory compliance with agreed service SLAs. This
                Compensation may take the form of a fixed or variable amount
                ( <em>e.g. </em>a monthly amount in euros or tokens, or a bonus
                per validated block), as defined in the approved economic model
                by ISBE governance. </p>
<p>In any case, payment will be subject to the Participant having
                maintained the required availability and performance standards
                during the corresponding period. </p>
<p>Minor breaches could lead to proportional reductions
                in remuneration, while serious or repeated breaches
                may result in the total loss of compensation for that period and
                eventually the revocation of the role as Validator. </p>
<p>The exact conditions of remuneration (amount, frequency of payment,
                currency, method) will be detailed in an annexed document or table approved by
                the ISBE Board of Directors, which may review them periodically in
                depending on the available budget and the evolution of the network. </p>
<p>Any change in the remuneration policy will be notified to
                the Validators in advance and, if any Validator does not accept it, this
                may resign from the role without penalty. </p>
<p>All costs associated with the installation and maintenance of the Node
                of Consensus (equipment of <em>hardware </em>, Internet connection
                high availability, electricity consumption, services <em>cloud </em>yes
                applies, technical personnel) will be assumed entirely by the
                Participant. The compensation provided by ISBE is intended to help
                bear those costs, but the Participant understands that he or she may not
                cover them in their entirety. </p>
<p>Likewise, it is stated that any general rate of
                membership applicable to the Basic Participant Participation Level
                still applies to the Validator. That is, participation as
                Validator does not exempt from the payment of annual fees due to being
                Validator). </p>
<p>Collaboration as a Validator is voluntary and does not generate a relationship
                any employment with the Managing Entity or with the other participants; if
                It is a civil compensation for a technical service provided to the
                ecosystem. The Participant is free to organize human resources or
                technical resources intended to operate the Consensus Node, under its own
                responsibility. </p>
</li>
<li>
<h3><strong>Non-compliance with SLAs and sanctions: </strong></h3>
<p>If the Participant repeatedly fails to meet the performance metrics
                established performance (for example, it has low availability or high
                latency continuously), the Managing Entity may apply measures
                correctives. </p>
<p>Firstly, it will notify the Participant so that they can correct the
                deficiencies within a given period. If the problems persist, the
                Managing Entity may temporarily suspend the Consensus Node of the
                participation in consensus (passing it to <em>standby </em>or removing it from
                the list of active validators) and even revoke the condition of
                Validator of the Participant by terminating this annex by
                non-compliance. This revocation would preferably be done with the agreement
                of the Participant; otherwise it will be channeled through the
                forced withdrawal procedure provided for in the Framework Contract (and may
                lead to total expulsion if non-compliance seriously compromised
                the network). </p>
<p>Additionally, a Validator who repeatedly fails to comply with the
                established performance metrics may lose the right to
                compensation during the affected periods, as indicated. </p>
</li>
<li>
<h3><strong>Termination of the Validator role: </strong></h3>
<p>The Participant may voluntarily cease as Validator
                notifying it at least 1 month in advance so that the Entity
                Manager reorganize the consensus without its Consensus Node. After the
                deadline, you will be removed from the list of validators and will have no effect
                this annex, remaining as a Basic Participant or other Levels of
                Participation that you had, unless you requested total withdrawal. </p>
<p>In case of voluntary resignation, the Participant undertakes to
                cooperate in the transition, for example, by providing evidence of
                secure termination (key deletion, etc.). </p>
<p>The Managing Entity may finalize this annex if, due to changes
                structures in the network, the number of validators is reduced or
                modifies the consensus model. In this case, it will try to agree with
                the Participant transitions to an alternative role ( <em>e.g. </em>Observer)
                or voluntary withdrawal, as preferred, and will pay any compensation
                accrued until the date of termination. </p>
</li>
</ol>
</details>
